From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:24:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D220 server: a relative canonical project directory is
 rejected with 400

Upstream: PATCH /api/project/:id with {"canonical":"relative"} (or "") answers 500 with an empty body, for a known
or an unknown project. AbsolutePath is an unchecked brand, so the path reaches the project table's absolute-path
column, which throws before the update can find out that the project does not exist.
Fixed: 400 InvalidRequestError, field canonical, message "canonical must be an absolute path" (the shape D201
gives a relative session directory), checked before the project lookup as the payload schema would be.
Scenarios: project-projects.test.ts "update project metadata" (new requests)
Upstream tests: packages/server/test/project-update.test.ts (new)

